<!--
  The ONE localization surface for the shared Compose UI (UIUX-PLAN §1.4 / §4.6.4 D6 re-scope):
  English source values for EVERY UiEffect variant and all steps-1-8 chrome. The VM/contract layer
  stays display-text-free (D5/D6); this file plus ui/UiEffectMessages.kt are the sanctioned home of
  user-facing text in commonMain. compose-resources resolves the locale natively per platform
  (iOS rides the 1.12-beta02 NSLocale integration), so this single file serves desktop/android/ios
  (and the web plan) without per-platform strings.xml / String Catalog / web-i18n triplication.

  Conventions:
  - Positional format args (%1$s / %1$d), resolved via the suspend getString(Res.string.…, args).
  - Singular/plural pairs are explicit *_one / *_other string pairs picked in the exhaustive `when`
    (UiEffectMessages.kt), mirroring the count == 1 branch of the retired App.kt toDisplayMessage().
  - Semantic-key effects (JobFailed / OperationFailed) get one localized template PER KNOWN KEY plus
    a generic fallback: raw developer keys ("VeoAsyncJob", "editWordAlignment") never reach the user.
  - Staged status labels are honest stage descriptions, never fake percentages (UIUX-PLAN §1.6/§2.5).
  - Import copy is media-neutral by design (E4/E5): "Import directory", never "audio importer", and
    no promise of video/image ingest, because the mp4 import arm is commented out (WVM:256-258) and
    the png arm is empty (WVM:260-261) — the copy must not advertise what the pipeline does not do.
-->
<resources>

